{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_product_is_link_polynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_product_is_link_polynomial","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L173-L186","doc":"**Constituent product equals the link polynomial** — derived:\nchaining the agreement identity with the definitional link\n`P_K(q) = tr_M(ρ(β_𝔥))` gives the outer equality of the manuscript\ndisplay, `∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ^const = P_{K_𝔥}(q)`.  Genuine composition of the\nmain claim with a definitional link, not a projected field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L133-L171","doc":"**Constituent/composite Markov-trace agreement**\n([`lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement`]) — proved sorry-free:\n\n  `∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ^const = tr_M(ρ(β_𝔥))`,\n\ni.e. Markov-trace multiplicativity across the constituent\nfactorisation of the hadron braid word.  The aggregate is obtained by\ninducting the per-constituent Markov peel (`peel`) over the prefix\nlength; the definitional links `constituent_product_def` /\n`composite_trace_def` / `partial_full` reduce the claim to that\naggregate. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","label":"lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tmli-constituent-composite-agreement.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.peel","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L129-L129","doc":"**One Markov peel per constituent** (`thm:markov-trace-product`\napplied at each interface): appending constituent `k` multiplies the\nrunning Markov trace by `tr_M(ρ(β_k))`.  Per-step *structural* input;\nthe aggregate agreement is **derived** from it below (§3b-cond item 5,\nnon-degenerate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partial_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partial_full","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L123-L123","doc":"Closure of the peel: the full partial composite over all `m`\nconstituents is the composite hadron braid image `ρ(β_𝔥)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L120-L120","doc":"Base of the Markov peel: the empty partial composite traces to `1`\n(`tr_M(𝟙) = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partialComposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.partialComposite","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The Markov-peel partial composites: `partialComposite k` is the\ncomposite Hecke element of the first `k` constituents along Jones's\nconstituent factorisation of `β_𝔥`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.P_K_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.P_K_def","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L113-L113","doc":"Definitional link: the link polynomial of the hadron knot is the\nMarkov trace of the composite braid image (Jones's construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.P_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.P_K","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The link-polynomial value `P_{K_𝔥}(q) : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.composite_trace_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.composite_trace_def","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Definitional link: `composite_trace = tr_M(ρ(β_𝔥))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.composite_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.composite_trace","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L106-L106","doc":"The composite Markov-trace value `tr_M(ρ(β_𝔥)) : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent_product_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent_product_def","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L103-L103","doc":"Definitional link: the constituent product is the product of the\ntraced constituent volumes over the `m` constituents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent_product","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The constituent product `∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ^const : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.V_hat_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.V_hat_def","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Definitional link: `V̂ᵢ^const = tr_M(ρ(β_i))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.V_hat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.V_hat","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Traced constituent volumes `V̂ᵢ^const : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.beta_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.beta_H","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Composite Hecke element `ρ(β_𝔥) ∈ H_N(R, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.constituent","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Constituent Hecke elements `ρ(β_i) ∈ H_N(R, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.m","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Number of constituents of the hadron `𝔥`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.TmliConstituentCompositeAgreementContext","kind":"class","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean#L78-L131","doc":"Data of the constituent/composite Markov-trace agreement claim, over\ngenuine ring/algebra **instance binders** (see the base-ring note in\nthe module docstring).  All fields are *inputs*: the hadron's braid\ndata, its traced values (pinned by definitional links), and the\nper-step Markov-peel factorisation of `β_𝔥`; none is the agreement\nconclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}